.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526061340/wu-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7.bin","sha256":"88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7"}},{"id":"ea16d75857a48c620f80200e5a35ab8a41a4ebe79987bf8a47fe2531002e9cc0","quote":"Other intangible assets primarily consist of software, contract costs (amounts paid to agents in connection with establishing and renewing long-term contracts), and acquired contracts. Other intangible assets are generally amortized on a straight-line basis over the length of the contract or benefit period. Included in the Consolidated Statements of Income is amortization expense of $130.2 million, $141.7 million, and $144.5 million for the years ended December 31, 2025, 2024, and 2023, respectively.","context":"Other Intangible Assets","section":"Business Combinations","block":1036,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-061340","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526061340/wu-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7.bin","sha256":"88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7"}},{"id":"b2bce46b956d3acfe77645560b05436dc67d6a673fb83c2660462eb5ca394562","quote":"The Company purchases and develops software that is used in providing services and in performing administrative functions. For developed software, the Company capitalizes the eligible costs (predominantly detailed design, development, and testing) incurred during the application development stage, and all other costs are expensed as incurred. Once the software is ready for its intended use, software development costs and purchased software are generally amortized over a term of three to seven years.","context":"Other intangible assets primarily consist of software, contract costs (amounts paid to agents in connection with establishing and renewing long-term contracts), and acquired contracts. Other intangible assets are generally amortized on a straight-line basis over the length of the contract or benefit period. Included in the Consolidated Statements of Income is amortization expense of $130.2 million, $141.7 million, and $144.5 million for the years ended December 31, 2025, 2024, and 2023, respectively.","section":"Business Combinations","block":1037,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-061340","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526061340/wu-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7.bin","sha256":"88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7"}},{"id":"e340f683eb4ece67b27f35c10413f6d41e0388312f6fdccb92e35deeda601885","quote":"The Company capitalizes initial payments for new and renewed agent contracts to the extent recoverable through future operations or penalties in the case of early termination. The Company’s accounting policy is to limit the amount of capitalized costs for a given contract to the lesser of the estimated future cash flows from the contract or the termination fees the Company would receive in the event of early termination of the contract. Capitalized contract costs are generally amortized over a term of five to ten years.","context":"The Company purchases and develops software that is used in providing services and in performing administrative functions. For developed software, the Company capitalizes the eligible costs (predominantly detailed design, development, and testing) incurred during the application development stage, and all other costs are expensed as incurred. Once the software is ready for its intended use, software development costs and purchased software are generally amortized over a term of three to seven years.","section":"Business Combinations","block":1038,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-061340","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526061340/wu-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7.bin","sha256":"88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7"}},{"id":"5b99352353153718f9d609dc75fb4d36efe1df48e9faa7bb13e1e09007af7cec","quote":"Acquired contracts include customer and contractual relationships and networks of subagents that are recognized in connection with the Company’s acquisitions.","context":"The Company capitalizes initial payments for new and renewed agent contracts to the extent recoverable through future operations or penalties in the case of early termination. The Company’s accounting policy is to limit the amount of capitalized costs for a given contract to the lesser of the estimated future cash flows from the contract or the termination fees the Company would receive in the event of early termination of the contract. Capitalized contract costs are generally amortized over a term of five to ten years.","section":"Business Combinations","block":1039,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-061340","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526061340/wu-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840eac6a7563ee12de2e54be86837ecc32d7.bin","sha256":"88b5a306884ba3d76d10766b1f35840